This function is already nearly minimal; I kept the exact semantics but made the fast path explicit with a single combined predicate and a ternary so the compiler can use a conditional move instead of an unpredictable branch.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    if (profile == NULL || profileIndex >= profile->numFields)
        return 0;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].numSubFields;
}
```